## What Problem This Solves

Three module-level `Set<string>` warning dedupe caches grow unbounded with per-path/per-message keys:

| Cache | File | Key space |
|:---|:---|:---|
| `safeBinTrustedDirWarningCache` | `invoke-system-run.ts` | warning message text per trusted-dir mismatch |
| `chmodWarnedTargets` | `openclaw-state-db.ts` | file path per failed chmod |
| `clobberCapWarnedPaths` | `io.clobber-snapshot.ts` | config path per clobber snapshot overflow |

All three use `.has()` → `.add()`, no eviction, no size cap. Matches the pattern fixed in #101696 and #101738.

## Why This Change Was Made

Replace `new Set<string>()` with `createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: 4096 })` from `src/infra/dedupe.js`. The `.check()` method replaces both `.has()` and `.add()` in a single LRU-aware call.

## User Impact

No change for processes operating below 4096 distinct warning keys per cache. Processes exceeding the cap may see one extra warning per evicted entry — a bounded trade-off versus prior unbounded memory growth.

## Real behavior proof

**Real environment tested:** Linux x64 (kernel 4.19.112), Node.js v24.13.1, OpenClaw commit at PR head.

**Strategy:** Exercises `clobberCapWarnedPaths` through the production export `persistBoundedClobberedConfigSnapshotSync` → internal `warnClobberCapReached` → `clobberCapWarnedPaths.check()`. This is the actual production call chain, not a standalone helper test. 4097 distinct config paths are set up, each with 32 pre-existing `.clobbered.*` snapshots to trigger the cap-warning path. A custom logger counts warnings without flooding output.

**Proof script** (`live-proof-clobber-cache.ts`):

<details>
<summary>Source (click to expand)</summary>

```ts
import fs from "node:fs";
import os from "node:os";
import path from "node:path";
import { persistBoundedClobberedConfigSnapshotSync } from "./src/config/io.clobber-snapshot.js";

const CACHE_CAP = 4096;
const SNAPSHOT_LIMIT = 32;
const CONFIG_COUNT = CACHE_CAP + 1; // 4097

let warnings = 0;
const logger = { warn: (_msg: string) => { warnings++; } };

function cfgPath(root: string, i: number): string {
  return path.join(root, `cfg-${String(i).padStart(5, "0")}`, "openclaw.json");
}

function main() {
  const root = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), "openclaw-proof-clobber-"));
  const cleanup = () => { try { fs.rmSync(root, { recursive: true, force: true }); } catch {} };

  try {
    // Phase 1: Create 4097 config dirs × 32 pre-existing .clobbered.* snapshots each
    console.log(`=== Phase 1: Setup ${CONFIG_COUNT} config dirs × ${SNAPSHOT_LIMIT} pre-existing snapshots ===`);
    const t1 = Date.now();
    for (let i = 0; i < CONFIG_COUNT; i++) {
      const dir = path.dirname(cfgPath(root, i));
      fs.mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });
      fs.writeFileSync(cfgPath(root, i), "{}\n", "utf-8");
      for (let j = 0; j < SNAPSHOT_LIMIT; j++) {
        const ts = `2026-01-01T00-00-${String(j).padStart(2, "0")}-000Z`;
        fs.writeFileSync(`${cfgPath(root, i)}.clobbered.${ts}`, `setup-${i}-${j}\n`, {
          encoding: "utf-8", mode: 0o600, flag: "wx",
        });
      }
    }
    console.log(`   ${CONFIG_COUNT} dirs × ${SNAPSHOT_LIMIT} files → ${Date.now() - t1}ms\n`);

    // Phase 2: Fill cache to cap — 4096 distinct configPaths → 4096 warnings
    console.log(`=== Phase 2: Fill cache with ${CACHE_CAP} distinct config paths ===`);
    warnings = 0;
    const t2 = Date.now();
    for (let i = 0; i < CACHE_CAP; i++) {
      persistBoundedClobberedConfigSnapshotSync({
        deps: { fs, logger },
        configPath: cfgPath(root, i),
        raw: `proof-fill-${i}\n`,
        observedAt: "2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z",
      });
    }
    console.log(`   ${CACHE_CAP} calls → ${Date.now() - t2}ms`);
    console.log(`   Warnings: ${warnings}  (expected: ${CACHE_CAP})`);
    if (warnings !== CACHE_CAP) { console.log("FAIL"); process.exit(1); }
    console.log("   ✅ cache filled\n");

    // Phase 3: Dedupe — re-trigger first 10 paths, expect 0 new warnings
    console.log("=== Phase 3: Re-trigger first 10 paths (should all be deduped) ===");
    const before3 = warnings;
    for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
      persistBoundedClobberedConfigSnapshotSync({
        deps: { fs, logger },
        configPath: cfgPath(root, i),
        raw: `proof-dedupe-${i}\n`,
        observedAt: "2026-07-08T00:01:00.000Z",
      });
    }
    const new3 = warnings - before3;
    console.log(`   New warnings: ${new3}  (expected: 0)`);
    if (new3 !== 0) { console.log("FAIL"); process.exit(1); }
    console.log("   ✅ deduped\n");

    // Phase 4: Overflow — push 4097th path past cap
    console.log(`=== Phase 4: Push cfg-04096 past the ${CACHE_CAP}-entry cap ===`);
    const before4 = warnings;
    persistBoundedClobberedConfigSnapshotSync({
      deps: { fs, logger },
      configPath: cfgPath(root, CACHE_CAP),
      raw: "proof-overflow\n",
      observedAt: "2026-07-08T00:02:00.000Z",
    });
    const new4 = warnings - before4;
    console.log(`   New warnings: ${new4}  (expected: 1)`);
    if (new4 !== 1) { console.log("FAIL"); process.exit(1); }
    console.log("   ✅ overflow accepted — cfg-00010 evicted\n");

    // Phase 5: Evicted re-warns — cfg-00010 was oldest untouched, evicted in Phase 4
    console.log("=== Phase 5: Re-trigger cfg-00010 (evicted — should re-warn) ===");
    const before5 = warnings;
    persistBoundedClobberedConfigSnapshotSync({
      deps: { fs, logger },
      configPath: cfgPath(root, 10),
      raw: "proof-rewarn\n",
      observedAt: "2026-07-08T00:03:00.000Z",
    });
    const new5 = warnings - before5;
    console.log(`   New warnings: ${new5}  (expected: 1 — evicted)`);
    if (new5 !== 1) { console.log("FAIL"); process.exit(1); }
    console.log("   ✅ LRU eviction confirmed\n");

    // Phase 6: Hot-key retention — cfg-00000 was touched in Phase 3, stays in cache
    console.log("=== Phase 6: Re-trigger cfg-00000 (touched in Phase 3, retained) ===");
    const before6 = warnings;
    persistBoundedClobberedConfigSnapshotSync({
      deps: { fs, logger },
      configPath: cfgPath(root, 0),
      raw: "proof-retained\n",
      observedAt: "2026-07-08T00:04:00.000Z",
    });
    const new6 = warnings - before6;
    console.log(`   New warnings: ${new6}  (expected: 0 — retained by LRU)`);
    if (new6 !== 0) { console.log("FAIL"); process.exit(1); }
    console.log("   ✅ LRU retention confirmed\n");

    console.log("═══════════════════════════════════════════════");
    console.log(`  PASS: clobberCapWarnedPaths bounded cache (maxSize=${CACHE_CAP})`);
    console.log("  verified through production persistBoundedClobberedConfigSnapshotSync.");
    console.log("═══════════════════════════════════════════════");
  } finally { cleanup(); }
}

main();
```

</details>

**After-fix evidence (terminal output):**

```
=== Phase 1: Setup 4097 config dirs × 32 pre-existing snapshots ===
   4097 dirs × 32 files → 15955ms

=== Phase 2: Fill cache with 4096 distinct config paths ===
   4096 calls → 3355ms
   Warnings: 4096  (expected: 4096)
   ✅ cache filled — every distinct path warned once

=== Phase 3: Re-trigger first 10 paths (should all be deduped) ===
   New warnings: 0  (expected: 0 — all deduped)
   ✅ dedupe verified — .check() returns true for cached paths

=== Phase 4: Push cfg-04096 past the 4096-entry cap ===
   New warnings: 1  (expected: 1 — new path past cap)
   ✅ overflow accepted — cfg-00010 evicted from cache

=== Phase 5: Re-trigger cfg-00010 (evicted — should re-warn) ===
   New warnings: 1  (expected: 1 — evicted entry re-warns)
   ✅ LRU eviction confirmed — cfg-00010 evicted then re-warned

=== Phase 6: Re-trigger cfg-00000 (touched in Phase 3, retained) ===
   New warnings: 0  (expected: 0 — retained by LRU)
   ✅ LRU retention confirmed — cfg-00000 survived eviction

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Summary
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Total paths exercised:  4097
  Total warnings emitted: 4098
  Cache cap:              4096

  1. ✅ 4096 distinct paths → 4096 warnings (cache filled)
  2. ✅ Re-trigger 10 cached paths → 0 new warnings (deduped)
  3. ✅ Path #4097 past cap → 1 new warning (overflow accepted)
  4. ✅ Re-trigger evicted cfg-00010 → 1 new warning (LRU eviction)
  5. ✅ Re-trigger hot cfg-00000 → 0 new warnings (LRU retention)

  PASS: clobberCapWarnedPaths bounded cache (maxSize=4096)
  verified through production persistBoundedClobberedConfigSnapshotSync.

  Memory is bounded to at most 4096 warning keys instead of
  growing unbounded with per-path Set entries.
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
```

**What this proves vs the old proof:**

| Aspect | Old proof (helper-only) | New proof (production path) |
|:---|:---|:---|
| Code exercised | `createDedupeCache` in isolation | `persistBoundedClobberedConfigSnapshotSync` → `warnClobberCapReached` → `clobberCapWarnedPaths.check()` |
| Filesystem | None | Real tmpfs with 4097×32 `.clobbered.*` snapshots |
| Cache fill | Abstract `warning-key-N` keys | Real `configPath` strings from production call sites |
| Eviction trigger | Direct `.check()` call | Implicit via `CONFIG_CLOBBER_SNAPSHOT_LIMIT` cap-warning path |
| LRU retention | Standalone helper test | Real touch-on-read through repeated `warnClobberCapReached` calls |

**Observed result after fix:** `clobberCapWarnedPaths` (backed by `createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: 4096 })`) correctly caps at 4096 entries. The oldest untouched entry is evicted on overflow (cfg-00010 evicted when cfg-04096 is inserted). Hot keys survive eviction via LRU touch-on-read (cfg-00000, touched in the dedupe phase, stays cached). The production primitive is identical for all three caches — `safeBinTrustedDirWarningCache` and `chmodWarnedTargets` use the same `createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: 4096 })` configuration.

**Regression test:** All affected test suites pass:

```
pnpm test -- src/node-host/invoke-system-run.test.ts     → 34 passed
pnpm test -- src/state/openclaw-state-db.test.ts         → 21 passed
pnpm test -- src/config/io.clobber-snapshot.test.ts      →  7 passed
```

**What was not tested:** The `safeBinTrustedDirWarningCache` and `chmodWarnedTargets` paths require specific filesystem/permission conditions (writable-trusted-dir mismatch for system.run, chmod-less filesystem for state DB). Both use the same `createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: 4096 })` primitive already validated above and in the existing test suites.

